   </property>
   <property name="text">
    <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Now our mixing stage! Luckily, Cachaca is pretty simple. The only ingredients you need are yeast and the sugarcane juice. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;There can be many different yeasts used during this process (such as CA-11, Canamax, and even yeaster from the field), but each will have a significant impact on the end flavor.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;The juice is completely fresh and is extracted within the first 24 hours after harvest of the sugarcane. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Once everything is mixed, and the sugar is the juice has been cleared, the cachaca has about 7-9% alcohol.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
   </property>
